* SHOW - CP/M 3 SYSTEM/DISK STATUS

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

A - Purpose, syntax and examples

:A
* SHOW - CP/M 3 SYSTEM/DISK STATUS

SYSOP ONLY. Private utility; use the local sysop console.

Syntax:
    SYSUTLS:SHOW [drive:] [options]

Displays CP/M status and disk information. Examples: SYSUTLS:SHOW I:
[SPACE] and SYSUTLS:SHOW [USERS]

Other CP/M 3 forms show disk labels, directory space and active RSX
modules. This is the DRI utility, distinct from SYSUTLS:ZSHOW, which
inspects the Z-System environment.

See HELP COMMANDS for the command index.
